  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **My Rag**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Nashville Blues**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **Cocaine Blues**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **You Won't Be Satisfied That Way**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- **I'm Alabama Bound**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Way Down The River Road**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Salty Dog**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n- **Rose Of Old Kentucky**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Black Mountain Rag [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2015-11-05.matrix.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 14 songs; 50 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2015-11-05.matrix.flac24**: taped by Mark Burgin; source: matrix [1]. Also: Matrix of a soundboard feed and a DIN stereo mic pair, run through Grace Design Lunatec V2 preamp into a Sound Devices 744t recorder; Mics were Busman Audio K23 hypercardioids through BST54 tubes, placed about 40 feet from stage and 10 feet high, recorded 24-bit/48 kHz; Edited in Magic Samplitude Pro X: mixed to stereo, normalized, with EQ and compression applied [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by SoundCloud: [I'm Alabama Bound](https://soundcloud.com/billystrings/im-alabama-bound) [5]",
